@prefix bot: <https://w3id.org/bot#> .
@prefix ifc: <http://ifcowl.openbimstandards.org/IFC4_ADD2#> .
@prefix orcid: <https://orcid.org/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix sssom: <https://w3id.org/sssom/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/000> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Both denote the area of land on which construction takes place. Not exact: IfcSite is an IfcProduct that can carry placement, geometry and a compositionType (COMPLEX/ELEMENT/PARTIAL), while bot:Site is a purely topological zone with no geometric commitment. Every IfcSite instance is defensibly a bot:Site; a bot:Site need not satisfy IfcSite's product-layer machinery." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcSite ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcSite" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Site ;
    sssom:subject_label "Site" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/001> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct. Same caveat as Site on the product-layer asymmetry. Note IFC 4.3 generalises IfcBuilding under IfcFacility (bridges, roads, marine works); IFC4 ADD2 has no IfcFacility, so infrastructure assets have no home on the IFC side of this pair while bot:Building is explicitly buildings only. The gap is symmetric and honest here; it stops being honest in Uniclass, which classifies bridges as entities alongside buildings." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcBuilding ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcBuilding" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Building ;
    sssom:subject_label "Building" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/002> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct. Both are the horizontal level-of-a-building notion, both sit strictly below Building in the containment hierarchy." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcBuildingStorey ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcBuildingStorey" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Storey ;
    sssom:subject_label "Storey" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/003> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Both are the bounded three-dimensional extent notion. IfcSpace requires association to the spatial structure and supports internal/external designation; bot:Space is any limited three-dimensional extent defined physically or notionally. bot:Space also plausibly covers IfcExternalSpatialElement, which IfcSpace excludes." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.85 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcSpace ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcSpace" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Space ;
    sssom:subject_label "Space" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/004> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "The structural mirror at the top of both hierarchies: bot:Zone subsumes Site, Building, Storey and Space exactly as IfcSpatialStructureElement subsumes IfcSite, IfcBuilding, IfcBuildingStorey and IfcSpace. Two independent committees drew the same four-way partition of built space. This, not any label match, is where the crosswalk starts." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.85 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcSpatialStructureElement ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcSpatialStructureElement" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Zone ;
    sssom:subject_label "Zone" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/005> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "IfcSpatialZone (new in IFC4) is a non-hierarchical spatial volume for thermal, lighting or accessibility zoning that may span storeys. It is one narrower kind of bot:Zone. Kept separate from the IfcSpatialStructureElement row because IfcSpatialZone sits outside the IfcSpatialStructureElement branch." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.7 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcSpatialZone ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcSpatialZone" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:narrowMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Zone ;
    sssom:subject_label "Zone" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/006> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Both denote the physically existing component with a characteristic technical function, form or position. Not promotable to equivalence: IFC subsumes IfcVirtualElement (a non-physical boundary placeholder) under IfcElement, and bot:Element carries no such member. See the asserted non-mapping below and DIVERGENCES.md D2." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.85 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcElement ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcElement" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Element ;
    sssom:subject_label "Element" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/007> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "IfcRelSpaceBoundary reifies the boundary between a space and an element, which is one narrower kind of bot:Interface. bot:Interface also qualifies zone-zone and element-element junctions (a thermal bridge between two walls) for which IFC4 offers no first-class object. The direction matters: read this row as 'IfcRelSpaceBoundary is the narrower concept'." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.7 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcRelSpaceBoundary ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcRelSpaceBoundary" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:narrowMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Interface ;
    sssom:subject_label "Interface" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/008> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "THE false friend of the pair, and the reason label-driven alignment fails here. IfcZone is not a spatial thing at all: it is a subclass of IfcGroup, an arbitrary non-spatial grouping of IfcSpace/IfcSpatialZone instances with no geometry and no containment semantics. bot:Zone is the spatial superclass of site, building, storey and space. Asserting bot:Zone = IfcZone drags every BOT site, building and storey into IFC's group branch. Same word, disjoint intent. See DIVERGENCES.md D1." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.95 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcZone ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcZone" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:predicate_modifier "Not" ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Zone ;
    sssom:subject_label "Zone" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/009> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "IfcVirtualElement exists to delimit a space where no physical element exists (an imaginary boundary splitting an open-plan floor). It has no technical function, no form and no material presence, so it fails bot:Element's definition even though IFC itself files it under IfcElement. See DIVERGENCES.md D2." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcVirtualElement ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcVirtualElement" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:predicate_modifier "Not" ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Element ;
    sssom:subject_label "Element" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc/mapping/010> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Tempting because both talk about two things meeting. IfcRelConnectsElements asserts physical/logical connectivity as a relationship instance; bot:Interface reifies the qualified surface or junction itself so that properties (thermal transmittance, fire rating) can attach to it. A connectivity assertion and a qualified junction are different ontological categories: one is a statement, the other is a thing." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.8 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcRelConnectsElements ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcRelConnectsElements" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:predicate_modifier "Not" ;
    sssom:subject_id bot:Interface ;
    sssom:subject_label "Interface" .

bot:Building skos:closeMatch ifc:IfcBuilding .

bot:Site skos:closeMatch ifc:IfcSite .

bot:Space skos:closeMatch ifc:IfcSpace .

bot:Storey skos:closeMatch ifc:IfcBuildingStorey .

bot:Element skos:closeMatch ifc:IfcElement .

bot:Interface skos:narrowMatch ifc:IfcRelSpaceBoundary .

bot:Zone skos:closeMatch ifc:IfcSpatialStructureElement ;
    skos:narrowMatch ifc:IfcSpatialZone .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> a sssom:MappingSet ;
    rdfs:label "W3C BOT (Building Topology Ontology) to ifcOWL IFC4 ADD2 crosswalk" ;
    rdfs:comment "Candidate-for-review crosswalk between the W3C Linked Building Data Community Group's Building Topology Ontology and ifcOWL IFC4 ADD2 (ISO 16739-1). Rows with predicate_modifier=Not are asserted NON-mappings: pairs that look alignable and are not. See DIVERGENCES.md. SKOS mapping direction follows the SKOS Reference: A skos:broadMatch B asserts B is the broader concept; A skos:narrowMatch B asserts B is the narrower concept. Confidence is the curator's, not a computed score." ;
    sssom:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/bot-ifc> ;
    sssom:mapping_set_version "0.1.0" .

